        <strong style="display: block; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #000000; margin-bottom: 8px;">Quick Answer: Why Does Google Maps Underestimate Moroccan Driving Times?</strong>
        <p style="font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(0,0,0,0.85); margin: 0;">
          Google Maps calculates Moroccan driving times using maximum statutory highway speed limits without accounting for reality on the ground: single-lane mountain switchbacks over 2,260-meter passes, slow-moving phosphate trucks, agricultural tractors, Gendarmerie radar checkpoints, and livestock crossings. For mountain and desert routes (such as <strong>Marrakech to Merzouga</strong> or <strong>Fes to the Sahara</strong>), always <strong>add 25% to 40% to Google Maps' estimates</strong> to calculate realistic, comfortable journey times.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 1.25rem;">
        Open Google Maps, punch in <em>"Marrakech to Erg Chebbi Dunes, Merzouga"</em>, and the screen comfortably returns: <strong>8 hours and 35 minutes (560 km)</strong>. It seems ambitious, but doable in a single day—or so hundreds of exhausted travelers mistakenly believe each week.
      </p>

      <p>
        In reality, attempting this marathon sprint turns what should be an enchanting cultural crossing of North Africa into a grueling 11-hour endurance trial. By the time you navigate the hairpin bends of the High Atlas, crawl behind heavy lorries, clear rural police checkpoints, and stop for coffee and fuel, the sun has vanished beneath the horizon. You miss the golden sunset camel trek into camp, arriving exhausted in pitch darkness.
      </p>

      <p>
        At Roam Morocco, our chauffeurs navigate these mountain passes weekly. In this authority guide, we break down the <strong>exact realistic driving times</strong> between Morocco’s primary destinations, why digital maps mislead you, and how to structure your <a href="/morocco-10-day-itinerary.html"><strong>10-day Morocco road trip</strong></a> to savor every mile.
      </p>

